~ full_length_mirror

if not State.has_seen_full_length_mirror_dialogue:
	It's the full-length mirror your friends gifted you long ago.
	Looking at it makes you regret moving out of town.
	You try to remember if the glass was already shattered before you ended up in this place.
	Frankly, you could have easily thrown a heavy blunt object at it out of sheer frustration any time you were forced to see your own reflection.
	In a way, it’s a relief that you only see a fragmented, semi-transparent ghost of yourself now.
	...
	Wait. In one of the smaller shards, you notice something else.
	It's your actual body, fast asleep.
	How do you get back into it?
	You summon your little to non-existent intelligence to ponder the mechanics of soul-reentry.
	To no one's surprise, you come up with nothing.
	$> State.has_seen_full_length_mirror_dialogue = true

You decide to stop thinking before your brain hurts and keep looking around.

=> END